      "content": "Deferring this conversation until your child is \"older\" often feels unfair and damaging because gender identity often emerges in preschool years, and ignoring a child's genuine sense of self can lead to long-term confusion. While every family has a unique approach, completely ignoring a child's identity or enforcing rigid gender roles is widely considered outdated and potentially harmful by child development experts. The most supportive approach is to affirm the truth of your child's experience and model respect for all identities from an early age.",
